<body>
    <nav class="navbar">
        <div class="navbar-left">
            <h1 id="name">Optimum Planner</h1>
            <!-- <img id="image"
                src="https://img.freepik.com/premium-vector/bus-icon-vector-template-flat-design_925480-170.jpg"
                alt="Bus Icon" class="bus-icon"> -->
        </div>
        <div class="navbar-right">
            <a href="https://github.com/your-profile" target="_blank" class="icon github">
                <i class="fab fa-github"></i>
            </a>
            <a href="https://twitter.com/your-profile" target="_blank" class="icon twitter">
                <i class="fab fa-twitter"></i>
            </a>
            <a href="https://facebook.com/your-profile" target="_blank" class="icon facebook">
                <i class="fab fa-facebook"></i>
            </a>
        </div>
    </nav>


    <h1>
        Vehicle Routing Problem !
    </h1>

    <div class="text">
        The Vehicle Routing Problem (VRP) optimizes the routes of delivery trucks, cargo lorries, public transportation
        (buses, taxis and airplanes) or technicians on the road, by improving the order of the visits. This routing
        optimization heavily reduces driving time and fuel consumption compared to manual planning:
    </div>

    <div class="container">

        <form action="/add" method="post">

            <input type="text" name="location" id="location" class="location" placeholder="Enter your location address">
            <button class="btn">Submit</button>

        </form>
    </div>
    <div>
        <ul>
            <% for(let obj of info){ %>
                <li>
                    <%= obj.location %> : <%= obj.geometry.coordinates[0] %>, <%= obj.geometry.coordinates[1] %>
                </li>
                <% } %>
    </div>
    </ul>
    <hr>

    <h2>Distance Matrix</h2>
    <table border="1">

        <% distances.forEach(row=>{ %>
            <tr>
                <% row.forEach(cell=>{ %>
                    <td>
                        <%= cell %>
                    </td>
                    <% }) %>
            </tr>
            <% }) %>

    </table>

    <h2>Duration Matrix</h2>
    <table border="1">

        <% durations.forEach(row=>{ %>
            <tr>
                <% row.forEach(cell=>{ %>
                    <td>
                        <%= cell %>
                    </td>
                    <% }) %>
            </tr>
            <% }) %>

    </table>

</body>

</html>